    "reading": "Across 45389 transitions from 4 recordings the horizontal velocity never once exceeded 49.0 sub-pixels/frame: 0 frames are above the documented P-meter class of 72 and 13 are above the run class of 48. The sub-pixel identity is satisfied to a median ratio of 1.000-1.000 with the velocity at frame $t$ and 1.000-1.028 with the velocity at $t+1$, so the factor of two is not a unit convention. Section 4.2's vertical window of -80 to 64 is itself exceeded by the recordings, which reach -112.0 to 70.0 and sit outside it on up to 29.2% of frames. The exact integration identity of Section 4.1 holds to a median of 0.0000 px when position advances by the velocity at $t$, and 0.0625 px when it advances by the velocity at $t+1$ - the convention every implementation in this repository uses - while up to 6.4% of recorded frames mismatch by more than 1 px. The published estimate closest to the run class is published_gameplay_template_bound at 0.47% - the class the recordings can reach is the run class, not the P-meter class that every error column has been scored against."
